VALUES
  ('cs_suffolk_demographics', 'plc_suffolk', 'demographics', 'Demographics',
   'Governance [ edit ] Local government [ edit ] The coat of arms of Suffolk County Council Since 1974, Suffok has been a two-tier non-metropolitan county, meaning the provision of local government services is divided between a county council and district councils. &#91; 1 &#93; &#91; 2 &#93; The county has been divided into five districts since 2019: Babergh , East Suffolk , Ipswich , Mid Suffolk , and West Suffolk . &#91; 3 &#93; &#91; 4 &#93; Suffolk County Council is based in Ipswich and has 75 county councillors. It has been controlled by the Conservative Party since the 2017 Suffolk County Council election . &#91; 5 &#93; In 2026, the Government of the United Kingdom announced its intention to reorganise Suffolk into three unitary authority areas by April 2028. The new areas will be Western Suffolk, Eastern Suffolk, and Ipswich and South Suffolk. &#91; 6 &#93; History [ edit ] Historically, Suffolk was divided into four for the purposes of the courts of quarter sessions , which met at Beccles , Bury St Edmunds , Ipswich and Woodbridge . &#91; 7 &#93; In 1860, the Beccles, Ipswich and Woodbridge divisions were merged into an East Suffolk division, administered from Ipswich, and the Bury St Edmunds division became the West Suffolk division. &#91; 8 &#93; Under the Local Government Act 1888 , which established county councils, the two divisions formed the basis of the administrative counties of East Suffolk and West Suffolk . &#91; 9 &#93; The three unitary authority areas into which Suffolk is planned to be divided from 2028: Western Suffolk Central and Eastern Suffolk Ipswich and South Suffolk On 1 April 1974, under the Local Government Act 1972 , East Suffolk (with the exception of five parishes and parts of two more, which were transferred to Norfolk), the county borough of Ipswich, and West Suffolk were merged to form a single non-metropolitan county of Suffolk. &#91; 1 &#93; The new county was originally divided into seven districts: Babergh, Forest Heath , Ip', '["clm_wiki_suffolk_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'places_ingest_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());

