VALUES
  ('cs_salisbury_geography', 'plc_salisbury', 'geography', 'Geography',
   'History [ edit ] Old Sarum [ edit ] .mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+span.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote,.mw-parser-output .hatnote+link+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}} Main articles: Old Sarum , Old Sarum Cathedral , and Old Sarum Castle A reconstruction of Old Sarum in the 12th century Salisbury viewed from Old Sarum The hilltop at Old Sarum lies near the Neolithic sites of Stonehenge and Avebury and shows some signs of early settlement. &#91; 1 &#93; It commanded a salient between the River Bourne and the Hampshire Avon , near a crossroads of several early trade routes. &#91; 2 &#93; During the Iron Age , sometime between 600 and 300&#160;BC, a hillfort ( oppidum ) was constructed around it. &#91; 2 &#93; The Romans may have occupied the site or left it in the hands of an allied tribe. At the time of the Saxon invasions , Old Sarum fell to King Cynric of Wessex in 552. &#91; 3 &#93; Preferring settlements in bottomland, such as nearby Wilton , the Saxons largely ignored Old Sarum until the Viking invasions led King Alfred (King of Wessex from 871 to 899) to restore its fortifications. &#91; 2 &#93; Along with Wilton, however, it was abandoned by its residents to be sacked and burned by the Dano - Norwegian king Sweyn Forkbeard in 1003. &#91; 4 &#93; It subsequently became the site of Wilton''s mint . &#91; 2 &#93; Following the Norman invasion of 1066, a motte-and-bailey castle was constructed by 1070. &#91; 2 &#93; The castle was held directly by the Norman kings; its castellan was generally also the sheriff of Wiltshire . In 1075 the Council of London established Herman as the first bishop of Salisbury , &#91; 5 &#93; uniting his former sees of Sherborne and Ramsbury into a single diocese which covered the counties of Dorset , Wiltshire, and Berkshir', '["clm_wiki_salisbury_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'places_ingest_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());

