VALUES
  ('plc_poughkeepsie', 'place', 'poughkeepsie', 'Poughkeepsie', 'published', 'en', 0,
   'Poughkeepsie is the largest city in, and county seat of, Dutchess County, New York, United States. It is surrounded by the Town of Poughkeepsie and had a population of 31,577 at the 2020 census, while the Kiryas Joel–Poughkeepsie–Newburgh metropolitan area has an estimated 712,000 residents. Poughkeepsie is in the Hudson Valley region, midway between the core of the New York metropolitan area and the state capital of Albany. It is served by the nearby Hudson Valley Regional Airport and Stewart International Airport in Orange County, New York.', unixepoch(), unixepoch());

