rticle by introducing more precise citations. ( July 2026 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) The Pascagoula (also Pascoboula , Pacha-Ogoula , Pascagola , Pascaboula , Paskaguna ) were an indigenous group living in coastal Mississippi on the Pascagoula River . The name Pascagoula is a Choctaw term meaning "bread eater". Choctaw native Americans using the name Pascagoula are named after the words for "bread eaters". &#91; 1 &#93; ^ Albert Gallatin A synopsis of the Indian tribes within th', '["clm_wiki_pascagoula_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
